=== Closed symmetric distance profiles ===
Both odd-index profile formulas checked for k=1,...,8 at every runner.

=== The 13-speed square-triangular row and hostiles ===
S_13=(P_1,...,P_13) has M=99/338 and profile numerators over 338:
  99,140,157,164,167,168,169,168,167,164,157,140,99
Replacing the central speed P_7=169 by 170 makes the proposed phase margin 35/169.
Including P_0=0 forces the maximum to zero; neither hostile inherits the theorem.

=== Scope ===
The Pell word is the deterministic silver continued fraction with digit 2, not Khinchin-typical data.
At N=13 the margin 99/338 is far above 1/14, so this is a structured safe family, not an LRC(14) frontier closure.
No planar-Jacobian carrier or variable polynomial Cohn factor is produced.
